{"id":"int-dd7c650e195ebe0ad07eef8434a2cf00","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-27T09:55:55.157945Z","actor":"Andreas Coroiu","issue_id":"pico-link-8v3.2.3","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"inreview","reason":"Merged to main as 8bb838f. hal_time_ms backed by embassy_time, nestable IRQ masking verified race-free by code review, dead hal_tick_ path deleted. BTstack 1000ms timer proven firing once per second over CDC on real hardware. The burst was a measurement artifact of the heartbeat counter only advancing while a host has the console open; the ~22-heartbeat dropped fire is expected 50ms-poll drift and is now documented in source."}}
{"id":"int-1013cbe0aeed8338ca13e7c072c0e396","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-27T10:06:20.173409Z","actor":"Andreas Coroiu","issue_id":"pico-link-8v3.2.2","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Superseded by pico-link-8v3.2.7 (2b-alt, embassy-usb CDC in pure Rust), which is closed and hardware-verified. Acceptance points 3 and 4 (CDC enumerates, boot line readable, picotool reboot -f -u into BOOTSEL with no button) were all met there. Point 2 (CFG_TUSB_MCU) was closed by the 2026-08-26 code review. Point 1 (link the RP2350 TinyUSB dcd) is MOOT: embassy-usb 0.6.0 owns the USB device peripheral (firmware-spike/Cargo.toml:18) and build.rs:99-143 keeps TinyUSB as a cross-compile probe only, no dcd. Linking the dcd would put two stacks on one peripheral. Consequence to carry forward: the eventual USB Audio Class sound card must be built on embassy-usb, not TinyUSB."}}
